 3. Meta debuts Muse Spark 1.3 
 
 By Ina Fried 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Meta released Muse Spark 1.3, an update it says significantly improves performance in coding and agentic tasks.

 Why it matters: Meta is trying to keep pace with Anthropic, OpenAI and Google, which all made major model announcements this week.

 State of play: Meta AI chief Alexandr Wang told Axios the update helps pave the way for upcoming products, such as personal agents.

 "It's very competitive with frontier models," Wang said in an interview. "A lot of the usability improvements that we've made will be really helpful for things that Mark [Zuckerberg] has talked about on earnings calls, like personal agents that can work 24/7 on your behalf and help you achieve your goals." The big picture: Meta's release comes amid a flurry of model updates from across the industry.

 Google yesterday debuted Gemini 3.8 Flash, as well as a version geared toward cybersecurity work. Google's new model showed some impressive performance on certain coding benchmarks, and a larger update, Gemini 4, remains in training. Anthropic released updates to its Fable and Mythos models designed to cut costs and reduce the frequency of refusals of user requests for safety issues. OpenAI, meanwhile, said it will soon release its Astra model, though it will limit its most powerful cybersecurity capabilities to a smaller group of testers. Keep reading. 

 
 
